            <ArticleTitle>Lead extractions: indications, procedural aspects, and outcomes.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>201-10</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.ccl.2013.12.005</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S0733-8651(13)00143-4</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>As a result of more cardiac implantable electronic devices being placed, a trend toward increasing device infections, and concerns regarding lead malfunction, there is an increased need for lead extraction skills and comprehensive lead management programs. This review discusses the current indications for lead extractions as well as the training requirements and tools and technology needed to create the foundation for a successful lead management program.</AbstractText>
